---
source: crates/psptool-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "render_help(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Inspect and modify AMD PSP firmware images.

Usage: psptool [OPTIONS] [FILE] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list         List directories and entries [aliases: ls]
  extract      Extract one or more entry bodies
  replace      Replace an entry body (and optionally re-sign)
  sign         Re-sign a signed entry with a caller-supplied private key
  verify       Walk every directory and report chain-of-trust verification status
  search-keys  Discover RSA pubkeys (structured + heuristic)
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [FILE]  Positional firmware image. Required for any action other than `--version` / no-args (which prints help)

Options:
  -V, --version
          Print version (mirrors upstream `-V` / `--version`)
  -E, --entries
          List entries — the upstream `-E` action (default when a `file` is supplied with no subcommand and no other action flag)
  -X, --extract-file
          Extract one or more entries — upstream `-X`
  -R, --replace-file
          Replace an entry's body — upstream `-R`
  -r, --rom-index <ROM_INDEX>
          Selector — ROM index inside a multi-ROM blob [default: 0]
  -d, --directory-index <DIRECTORY_INDEX>
          Selector — directory index inside the chosen ROM
  -e, --file-index <FILE_INDEX>
          Selector — entry index inside the chosen directory
  -T, --type-regex <TYPE_REGEX>
          Selector — type-name regex (alternative to `-d -e` for `-X`)
  -o, --outfile <OUTFILE>
          Output file (single-file `-X`/`-R`) or output directory (multi-file `-X`)
  -u, --decompress
          Decompress when extracting (`-X -u`). Errors when the entry is not compressed in single-file mode
  -c, --decrypt
          Decrypt when extracting (`-X -c`). Errors when the entry is not encrypted in single-file mode
  -k, --pem-key
          Emit the PEM-encoded pubkey (`-X -k`). Silently ignored for non-pubkey entries in multi-file mode
  -n, --no-duplicates
          Iterate unique entries only (`-E -n` / `-X -n`)
  -j, --json
          JSON output (`-E -j`)
  -t, --key-tree
          Print the certificate-tree key tree (`-E -t`)
  -m, --metrics
          Print parsing metrics (`-E -m`)
  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output. Adds the `flags / MD5 / size_signed / size_full / size_packed / load_addr` columns to `list`
  -s, --subfile <SUBFILE>
          Re-sign: replacement file contents (`-R -s`)
  -p, --privkey <PRIVKEY>
          Re-sign: private-key path (`-R -p`). When the upstream flag accepted a stub, this Rust port accepts a single PEM file [aliases: --privkeystub]
  -a, --privkeypass <PRIVKEY_PASS>
          Re-sign: passphrase for the private key (`-R -a`)
  -h, --help
          Print help
